{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors","id":482243,"title":"Werewolf Second Edition final version changes [and possible remaining errors!]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-16T06:06:57-07:00","id":482243,"title":"Werewolf Second Edition final version changes [and possible remaining errors!]","content":"As some of you might have noticed, the final version of Werewolf Second Edition was recently uploaded. I compiled a list of changes (excepting spelling, grammar and stat blocks), so I though I should share it. I won't guarantee completeness, but all the important changes are in here.<br /> <br /> The change also introduced a new error: on page 92 &quot;For example,&quot; should be removed under the Merits heading.<br /> <br /> Also Harmony is still imbalanced when considering Breaking Points. The lowest tier, 0-3 is four levels, while the highest tier, 8-10 is three levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Final edition changes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarified that not impossible to identify a werewolf in Hishu as supernatural (p.61).<br /> <br /> Initiative is Dexterity + Composure, not Dex + Wits (p.83).<br /> Speed is Species Factor + Strength + Dex, instead of Size + Strenght + Dex (p.83).<br /> <br /> Missing parts of Character Creation Quick Reference added (p.84).<br /> <br /> Clarification that a Totem cannot grant dots of Dedicated Locus or Totem, and that characters implied by social Mertis such as Allies or Retainer are not themselves part of the pack (p.92).<br /> [Error: under the heading Merits, &quot;For example,&quot; should be removed.)<br /> <br /> Rahu Hunter's Aspect inflicts Swaggering Condition instead of Submissive Condition (p.98).<br /> <br /> Facets of Shadow and Wolf Gifts are unlocked at any Renown increase (p.99).<br /> <br /> Essence can be gathered from a Locus by physically touching the heart in the physical realm, or eating strange bits of meat or vegetation that appear around the locus in Hisil, instead of the other way around (p.100).<br /> <br /> When creating a werewolf, pick a set of triggers instead of choosing individual ones. Also personal triggers are suffered at most once per night, while general triggers have no limit (p.103).<br /> <br /> For the third level of the Favored Form Merit, specialize in a Facet instead of a whole Gift (p.106).<br /> <br /> The drawback of Efficient Killer Merit is that use is a common kuruth trigger, instead of sending you straight into Wasu-Im (p.108).<br /> <br /> Auspice Renown is used in Clash of Wills of abilities that are not Gift Facets and thus have no associated renown (p.115).<br /> <br /> The Pack Triumphs Together Facet is now Reflexive instead of Instant (p.127).<br /> <br /> The Lore of the Land Facet has a dice pool of Intelligence + Survival + Purity (p.128).<br /> <br /> The area of the Ward the Wolf's Den Facet keys of Glory instead of Cunning (p.135).<br /> <br /> While under the effect of Chain Rage, achieving five turns of lucidity during a period of Wasu-Im ends the rage (p.140).<br /> <br /> Jumping is Strength + Athletics (p.161).<br /> <br /> Using Hard Leverage is a breaking point towards Flesh. Against humans it removes one Door if the character's Harmony is 8 or more. Used on spirits remove one Door if the character's Harmony is 2 or Less. Otherwise remove two Doors (p.164).<br /> <br /> Environment levels now go from 0 to 4 instead of 1 to 5 (p.173).<br /> <br /> Stun Gun has a +1 to +3 die bonus, instead of zero (p. 177).<br /> <br /> Instead of Resolve + Composure, spirits roll Power + Resistance when confronted with a bane (p.185).<br /> <br /> Defense is lower of Power and Finesse instead of Finesse and Resistance (p.185).<br /> <br /> Reference about spirits having to be of the same type to be eachother's banes removed (p.185).<br /> <br /> References to Angels and Ghosts removed from influence rules (p.187).<br /> <br /> Instead of Control, Strengthen upgrades Resonant to Open (p.189).<br /> <br /> Rapture inflicts a Condition instead of a Derangement (p.192).<br /> <br /> The Fire Elemental Dread Power costs 1 Essence and has a duration of one scene (p.210).<br /> <br /> Toxic Bite and Venomous Ichor do not inflict Sick Tilts anymore, only Poison (p.211).<br /> <br /> Essence Vemon inflicts Poisoned, and not Sick (p.218).<br /> <br /> Under the influence of Devil Inside, a Wolfblooded stays in Dalu until she leaves the scene, instead of flees the scene (p.301).<br /> <br /> Under Host-Ache, Concentration roll must be Composure roll (p.302).<br /> <br /> Anyone who fails their roll when entering an area marked by a Marker suffers the Demorized Condition, and not Driven Away (p.302).<br /> <br /> With Second Skin one can change into Urhan and not Urshul (p.303).<br /> <br /> Shape-Shifted turns you into Urshul and not Urhan (p.303).<br /> <br /> Moon Taint inflicts the Poisoned Tilt and not the Sick Tilt (p.309).<br /> <br /> Submissive Condition replaced by Swaggering, which has a different effect (p.311).<br /> <br /> Poisoned description changed so that it also accounts for sickness (p.313).</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Added the changes to choosing kuruth triggers and how often triggers can happen. Missed it on my first pass as the sidebar has a strange background color which my comparison program doesn't handle well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 04-16-2015, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:43:17-07:00","id":482277,"title":"","content":"Swaggering is terrible. A Rahu lashes out with the full force of his dominance or purity and... the target feels more confident?<br /> Fooling someone / making them act stupid does not feel like Rahu. That's Irraka.<br /> <br /> Good job adding Spontaneous Wolf Blooded to the Lunacy section.<br /> <br /> Good job clarifying that werewolves <b>&quot;pick one of the following sets of triggers&quot;</b> instead of picking and choosing from multiple lists.<br /> <br /> Good job clarifying how frequently a Kuruth Trigger can happen (edited).<br /> <br /> Good job clarifying Hishu form's advantage.<br /> <br /> Good job clarifying the Harmony table.<br /> <br /> Song in your Heart is still broken.<br /> <br /> Interesting change to Efficient Killer! We'll have to test this out!<br /> <br /> Hard Leverage causing a breaking point towards Flesh makes no sense.<br /> <br /> Really loving the revised character sheet. Awesome job, Mr. Gone!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 04-16-2015, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:48:56-07:00","id":482280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors#post482243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Clarified that not impossible to identify a werewolf in Hishu as supernatural (p.61).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see this mechanics in this ficition paragraph. Maybe it's later, in Hishu mechanics section clarified?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:52:05-07:00","id":482283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482280#post482280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not see this mechanics in this ficition paragraph. Maybe it's later, in Hishu mechanics section clarified?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in the Hishu mechanics, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:06:52-07:00","id":482287,"title":"","content":"I think swaggering works quite well. A Rahu has a bunch of other methods of cowing prey into submission, but getting them to overconfidently stroll into an ambush? That's useful for a warrior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:13:36-07:00","id":482291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482277#post482277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still no clarification on how frequently a Kuruth Trigger can happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>p 103: &quot;All of the general triggers affect every werewolf; though she only suffers her personal triggers once a night, general triggers have no such limit.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:22:53-07:00","id":482300,"title":"","content":"Once a night, let's say, twelve hours intervals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:59:42-07:00","id":482333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482291#post482291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p 103: &quot;All of the general triggers affect every werewolf; though she only suffers her personal triggers once a night, general triggers have no such limit.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like you are absolutely right! I failed my perception check. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482287#post482287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think swaggering works quite well. A Rahu has a bunch of other methods of cowing prey into submission, but getting them to overconfidently stroll into an ambush? That's useful for a warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics are good, but the flavor text is all wrong for a Rahu. It should read something like:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Challenged</b></u><br /> <b>Your character has been called out by the force of a Rahu's essence. He has been encouraged or shamed into immediately facing this challenge.</b> He cannot prepare himself to face the Rahu or her pack in any way \u2014 buying weapons, laying traps, or changing his normal routine \u2014 without first spending a Willpower point and making an extended, reflexive Resolve + Composure roll. You may make one roll per turn, but each roll requires an additional point of Willpower. The target number of successes is equal to the Rahu's Purity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:00:49-07:00","id":482336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482277#post482277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swaggering is terrible. A Rahu lashes out with the full force of his dominance or purity and... the target feels more confident?<br /> Fooling someone / making them act stupid does not feel like Rahu. That's Irraka.</div> </div> </div> </div>The condition was changed deliberately to bring it into line with the Auspice's description of the Rahu hunter's aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahu writeup</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter\u2019s Aspect: Dominant. The prey spoils for a fight. He has no idea that death is coming, he thinks he can win<br /> this. He sees the movement in the shadow as nothing he can\u2019t handle, and goes in search of satisfaction \u2014 mating, food, good company.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:10:02-07:00","id":482370,"title":"","content":"Thanks Penta for coming up with this list! We that have already started creating characters and statting up NPCs really appreciate what you've done here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":". 04-16-2015, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:46:43-07:00","id":482477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482280#post482280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not see this mechanics in this ficition paragraph. Maybe it's later, in Hishu mechanics section clarified?</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally the fiction paragraph conflicted with the mechanics, as it said that it was impossible to identify her as supernatural. This was removed in the final version, thereby eliminating the conflict.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482291#post482291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> p 103: &quot;All of the general triggers affect every werewolf; though she only suffers her personal triggers once a night, general triggers have no such limit.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems I managed to miss this change, and the change in choosing personal triggers. Added them to the original post. If someone else notices changes I've missed (that aren't layout, spelling, etc.) let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 04-16-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:00:24-07:00","id":482488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482477#post482477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally the fiction paragraph conflicted with the mechanics, as it said that it was impossible to identify her as supernatural. This was removed in the final version, thereby eliminating the conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked mechanics section, corrected in document. Now it does makes sense:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revised version</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Sheep\u2019s Clothing: Any efforts to pinpoint the werewolf in a crowd or pursue her through populated areas suffer her Primal Urge as a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Hishu do not conceal your supernatural nature, only it makes you blend in with the herd. Much more logical, and usefull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:48:53-07:00","id":482555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482488#post482488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I checked mechanics section, corrected in document. Now it does makes sense<br /> <br /> So Hishu do not conceal your supernatural nature, only it makes you blend in with the herd. Much more logical, and usefull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, the mechanics were already this way in the first version, but nice that it makes sense to you now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:59:04-07:00","id":482655,"title":"","content":"Lunacy doesn't mention what Urshul's modifier is, as far as I know? It still says &quot;See page 101&quot; but only mentions Dalu as +2 and Gauru as -2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T13:18:45-07:00","id":482672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mabs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482655#post482655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunacy doesn't mention what Urshul's modifier is, as far as I know? It still says &quot;See page 101&quot; but only mentions Dalu as +2 and Gauru as -2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had taken that to mean that Urshul doesn't have a modifier (or, more accurately, the modifier is +/- 0). Though a clarification would have been nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T13:32:41-07:00","id":482727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Facets of Shadow and Wolf Gifts are unlocked at any Renown increase (p.99). </div> </div> </div>There seems to be a contradiction in the updated text, unless I'm missing something.<br /> <br /> It says in the character creation section on page 83,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character receives the first dot of a Moon<br /> Gift according to her auspice. She also receives a Facet of two<br /> Shadow Gifts from her tribe or auspice. If she has two dots<br /> in her auspice\u2019s Renown, she gains the second-dot Facet of<br /> that Moon Gift. Otherwise, she gains a facet of a Wolf Gift. </div> </div> </div>Later, in the section on Renown, it states on page 99,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each time your character increases<br /> her auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift.<br /> Every time she increases any Renown, she gains a Facet of a<br /> Shadow or Wolf Gift. </div> </div> </div>The contradiction as I'm reading it lies in the use of the word &quot;otherwise&quot; in the character creation section. It implies that, if you use a creation renown dot to buy the second dot in your auspice renown, you <i>either</i> get a facet of your Moon gift <i>or</i> you get a Wolf gift facet, but you don't get both. However, later, the renown section implies that you get both your auspice Moon facet and a Shadow or Wolf gift. Essentially, if at character creation, you choose to put your third renown creation dot in your Auspice renown, and you choose a Wolf gift, you miss out on a Moon gift. A newly created character would be better off waiting to buy an auspice renown dot later with 3 XP to get two facets for the price of one. Is that as intended? Or is it clarified better elsewhere in the text, and I've glossed over it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5290-didion","user":"Didion","date":". 04-16-2015, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5290-didion","name":"Didion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T13:55:26-07:00","id":482742,"title":"","content":"Nah, if you get two auspice dots you get the moon gift. No wolf gift for you. Not that they're hard to get after the fact or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:01:29-07:00","id":482755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Didion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482727#post482727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be a contradiction in the updated text, unless I'm missing something.<br /> <br /> It says in the character creation section on page 83,<br /> <br /> <br /> Later, in the section on Renown, it states on page 99,<br /> <br /> <br /> The contradiction as I'm reading it lies in the use of the word &amp;quot;otherwise&amp;quot; in the character creation section. It implies that, if you use a creation renown dot to buy the second dot in your auspice renown, you <i>either</i> get a facet of your Moon gift <i>or</i> you get a Wolf gift facet, but you don't get both. However, later, the renown section implies that you get both your auspice Moon facet and a Shadow or Wolf gift. Essentially, if at character creation, you choose to put your third renown creation dot in your Auspice renown, and you choose a Wolf gift, you miss out on a Moon gift. A newly created character would be better off waiting to buy an auspice renown dot later with 3 XP to get two facets for the price of one. Is that as intended? Or is it clarified better elsewhere in the text, and I've glossed over it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting Renown and Gifts work slightly differently than those bought after character creation. At chargen, you get 2 shadow gift facets and the first dot of your moon gift no matter what. If you take a second dot on your auspice renown, you get the second dot of your moon gift. If you don't, you get a facet of a wolf gift. This way, you always start with 4 gift facets, and doubling up on your auspice renown isn't a cheap way to start with extra facets. After that, increasing any Renown gives you a free facet of that Renown type in a shadow gift you have unlocked, or any wolf gift. If it's your auspice renown, you also get the next dot in your moon gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:04:47-07:00","id":482758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482755#post482755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Starting Renown and Gifts work slightly differently than those bought after character creation. At chargen, you get 2 shadow gift facets and the first dot of your moon gift no matter what. If you take a second dot on your auspice renown, you get the second dot of your moon gift. If you don't, you get a facet of a wolf gift. This way, you always start with 4 gift facets, and doubling up on your auspice renown isn't a cheap way to start with extra facets. After that, increasing any Renown gives you a free facet of that Renown type in a shadow gift you have unlocked, or any wolf gift. If it's your auspice renown, you also get the next dot in your moon gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the lightbulb comes on! Thank you, Charlaquin, for the clarification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5290-didion","name":"Didion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T16:10:24-07:00","id":482894,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>Instead of Control, Strengthen upgrades Resonant to Open (p.189).&quot;</i><br /> <br /> That you can use Control to upgrade Open to Controlled is still missing from the Controlled Condition description, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T16:13:21-07:00","id":482900,"title":"","content":"As far as things go, that one does have the advantage of being Exactly What It Says On The Tin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:33:39-07:00","id":483632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=482900#post482900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as things go, that one does have the advantage of being Exactly What It Says On The Tin.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I like consistency in rules sets. If the use of Strengthen is mentioned in the Causing the Condition part of Open, then the use of Control should be mentioned in Causing the Condition of Controlled. Also, it being left out of Causing the Conditions can cause confusion. It not being there seems to contradict the Influences and Manifestations charts, so one might rightly wonder which is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T04:46:55-07:00","id":484408,"title":"","content":"In my revisioned PDF Merits are bookmarked under Triggers, when they should be a level higher on bookmarks tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:10:57-07:00","id":485509,"title":"","content":"Wolf Gift Facets are marked as costing 1 Experience on the QR chart on p84 and in the Gaining Gifts and Facets section on p115, but described as costing two Experiences in the Gifts and Rites paragraphs on p85.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-19-2015, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:30:46-07:00","id":485640,"title":"","content":"It was supposed to be fixed to say one xp in both sections. It's somewhere in the pages of the errata sticky thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:03:16-07:00","id":486484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=485640#post485640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was supposed to be fixed to say one xp in both sections. It's somewhere in the pages of the errata sticky thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, unlocking additional facets costs only 1 xp in even for shadow gifts?<br /> <br /> Can I get a reference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:15:44-07:00","id":486486,"title":"","content":"No, just for wolf gifts. Wolf gift facets always cost 1 experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:16:42-07:00","id":486487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482243-werewolf-second-edition-final-version-changes-and-possible-remaining-errors?p=486484#post486484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, unlocking additional facets costs only 1 xp in even for shadow gifts?<br /> <br /> Can I get a reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>What? No. 1 xp for Wolf Facets, 2 xp for Shadow Facets. &quot;Both sections&quot; refers to the section of the quick reference sheet where it (correctly) says Wolf Facets cost 1 xp and the section of page 85 where it (incorrectly) says Wolf Facets cost 2xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T18:08:52-07:00","id":486900,"title":"","content":"They're cheap to get, expensive to use compared to shadow Gifts (in general, I know some cost nothing like Father's form.) Wolf Gifts also seem like they would be better to get (more useful) after you've built up your character a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key"